e biden has  separate yourself from ideology  and separate yourself from what would be  the perfect  and analyze what is joe biden's platform  joe biden  would raise the corporate profit tax and  establish  what is effectively a minimum tax for  corporations similar to the alternative  minimum tax that people have had  since individuals have had since 1969.  that  is radical in a context where both  parties have allowed the zero  tax dollar status quo of corporations to  perpetuate itself  joe biden would eliminate deductions for  high-income earners  joe biden would repeal most of the trump  tax cuts and  increase taxes on fossil fuel emissions  so uh joe biden would uncap  starting at four hundred thousand  dollars the twelve  percent tax uh for social security  that is absolutely massive i actually  don't think for a moment i'm going to  imagine  it's not that people don't care it's  that people don't understand the  magnitude of that  you would see a ceo who earns 10 million  dollars a year  go from paying a 0.2 percent effective  social security tax to a 12 percent  effective social security tax that is a  massively radical proposal which you  will see  all sorts of people uh fight tooth and  nail to prevent  from becoming a reality and then joe  biden would take those revenues  and reinvest them in raising social  security benefits for the poor  that's exactly the type of policy that a  bernie sanders type  would put in place there are hundreds of  thousands of seniors who would be  immediately pulled out of poverty  as a result of that policy without it  costing the middle class  a penny some say a dime i say a penny  as we know capital gains is something  that allows  the super rich who don't work to pay  less as an effective tax rate than many  people who do work  capital gains long-term capital gains  taxed at a far  lower rate than earned income for the  rich  joe biden has proposed eliminating that  lower capital gains rate on dividends  and  long-term capital gains for everybody  making above  a million dollars per year if you  combine that  with raising the top tax rate back to  close to 40 percent  that is a combination of proposals from  joe biden  which would nearly double the average  tax rate for non-working  millionaires the tax policy center has  analyzed this proposal  and has found that three-quarters of joe  biden's tax increases  would fall on the one percent on the top  one percent  and a lot of that remaining 25 would  fall  on the top two to four percent this is  serious stuff  this is serious radical stuff the people  that then come in and say well he'll  never get it done  but hold on that that's not just joe  biden every president has trouble  getting done  what they want to do and you would have  to apply that exact same standard that  exact same logic that exact same caveat  to bernie sanders you can say well it's  not  left enough okay but say that and  recognize  that it would be the most progressive  economic policy  for a sitting president for a long long  time there will be people who come in  and say  but the top marginal tax rate was up in  the 90s during dwight d  eisenhower's presidency yes but the  amount of loopholes available at that  time and remember  the alternative minimum tax was not put  in place until 1969.  so prior to that even with these high  sticker tax rates under eisenhower  the very rich were rarely paying  anything close to that because of the  amount of loopholes and because of the  lack of  what's called the alternative minimum  tax so  you can critique joe biden in saying he  doesn't go far enough for example joe  biden wants to  reinstate some of those state and local  tax deductions  that donald trump got rid of there is no  doubt  that there are sort of medium wealthy  and super wealthy people in blue states  that lost some significant deductions  when trump  capped state and local tax deductions  and yes  both the democratic and republican party  are beholden 